    "translation": "To him, despairing in the middle of both of the two armies, O descendant of Bharata, the lord of the senses, as if smiling, spoke this word."
  },
  "11": {
    "words": [
      { "sa": "aśocyān", "en": "those not to be grieved for" },
      { "sa": "anvaśocaḥ", "en": "have grieved for" },
      { "sa": "tvam", "en": "you" },
      { "sa": "prajñā-vādān", "en": "words of wisdom", "term": "prajna" },
      { "sa": "ca", "en": "and" },
      { "sa": "bhāṣase", "en": "you speak" },
      { "sa": "gata-asūn", "en": "those whose breath has gone" },
      { "sa": "agata-asūn", "en": "those whose breath has not gone" },
      { "sa": "ca", "en": "and" },
      { "sa": "na", "en": "not" },
      { "sa": "anuśocanti", "en": "grieve for" },
      { "sa": "paṇḍitāḥ", "en": "the learned" }
    ],
    "translation": "You have grieved for those not to be grieved for, and you speak words of wisdom. The learned do not grieve for those whose breath has gone and those whose breath has not gone."
  },
